From e9802a1b7cc63f4ca6c69746ba39e2edc84cef73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 3 <phase3@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:10:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] c-family: match WCH .highcode section semantics

WCH 15.2.0 treats the exact, case-sensitive .highcode section as
non-inlinable and optionally appends the source declaration name when
--param=highcode-gen-section-name=1.  Match that named declaration
surface.

The change belongs in the front end rather than in the RISC-V back end
because that is where the observed surface is decided: the section name is
rewritten from DECL_NAME while the section attribute is handled, before
any target hook sees the declaration, and the official compiler performs
the same rewrite for variables as for functions, including a
function-local static.  The parameter is correspondingly a Common
parameter, which is what the whole-page --help=params comparison against
the official compiler shows.

The attribute handler admits only variable or function declarations.  A
bounded 30-shape C/C++ matrix found no accepted unnamed declaration and no
ICE in either the official or patched compiler.  The unguarded DECL_NAME
access therefore follows the observed front-end invariant; it is not
claimed as fidelity to an observed official ICE.

The 37-case official matrix matches in every field of RC01, the .highcode
repair round; the only two whole-page help differences are the parameter
of the separate RC05 ccv-abi round.  Directed DejaGnu has C 339 PASS and
C++ 3 PASS; the dual-lane suite diff retains every baseline PASS, the
selected EVT gate remains 274/274, and the RC01 full run has zero MATCH
regressions.

Behavior evidence:
